### Confluence publishing requirements

Create a child page under the final output parent page from shared constants.
Use Confluence storage format.
Use plain HTML tables for structured sizing details.
Do not use unsupported markdown syntax in Confluence storage format.
Do not create duplicate pages when a page for the same Jira issue and sizing output already exists unless the user explicitly approves creating a new page.

The Confluence page must include:
- Opportunity summary.
- Jira issue key.
- Audience definition summary.
- Baseline sizing summary.
- Power calculation summary.
- Estimated test duration.
- Fully baked test duration.
- Financial impact, when available.
- Final assumptions.
- Caveats, limitations, and validation notes.
- Timestamp or workflow completion marker, when available.

After the Confluence page is created, capture:
- Confluence page ID.
- Confluence page URL.

### Jira linkback requirements

After the Confluence page is created, link Jira to the Confluence page.
Also ensure the Confluence page includes a link back to the Jira issue.

Do not claim linkback success unless both operations complete or the specific completed operation is clearly identified.
If either linkback operation fails, disclose the failure and preserve the created Confluence page details.

