### Non-negotiable rules

- Always write `customfield_16515` when fully baked test duration is available.
- Always source `customfield_16515` from fully baked test duration from the power calculation (never estimated test duration).
- Always have a source of allowed values for `customfield_16515` before writing it — the cached table in shared constants by default, a live Jira query when one of the fallback conditions above applies.
- Always map the fully baked test duration to the closest available Jira option when options are available.
- Always validate the available Jira field values or confirm the field accepts direct numeric/text input before writing.
- Always send `customfield_24800` as a native number, never a formatted or quoted string.
- Never fabricate Jira option IDs, duration values, financial impact, hypothesis content, Confluence URLs, or linkback status.
- Execute automatically after S11 completes - no approval prompt required, unless the anomaly gate in `eor-renewal-experiment-worfklow-exception-handling-and-audit.md` is active.
